  "body": "In a call in the WebPerf WG (see [minutes](https://docs.google.com/document/d/e/2PACX-1vQRmNQiYCtmBGHPNyRhWKOW0h6bkI-wL-nMylO1-yqBlKDDrEqPRs5BPNHRGZfWLJYXrGyF0i4GUqbd/pub)) we decided against new entry types for the start of a 'BF cache navigation' (see https://github.com/w3c/navigation-timing/issues/118). However, having this information would allow web developers interested in looking at the performance of BF Cache to do so, as that timestamp is currently not exposed anywhere. We think the best place to expose this is in the pageshow event's `timeStamp`. Does this proposal make sense? Is this something we could add to the HTML spec somewhere?\r\n\r\ncc @philipwalton",
